Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-15-2001||04:04 AM||||Last I knew, Cliff wasn't importing them to the States yet.  As soon as he does, I'll contact my banker.  There are other kits out there.  AEX currently has the nicest set you can get in the States (IMO), but they are damn expensive!!!!!  Dolphin makes a set that are individual gauges, and you might try Dakota Digital, too.  They said that they could make me a set that would (approximately) fit in the stock area for less than a grand, but I wouldn't want to have to do that much modification to the dash.  Trial and error was never my strong suit.  (Well...error was.)<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||06-15-2001||04:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87 Pegasus:<BR><B>Where can i find one?  how much?  and how easy to install?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did'nt you see Pauls? He bought his cheaper than what PISA charges.<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">       </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||10
Z||000004||p4n1c||06-15-2001||08:51 AM||||If you want to do some dash work to make this fit, you can probably get it pretty cheap from a wreckers yard out of a '88-93(That's a guess I don't know when they stopped using this dash) Cutlass Supreme SL or International.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cutlass-dash-anim.gif"> <P>It'd probably be more suited for a custom dash sort of thing.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierogt88||06-15-2001||09:36 AM||||p4n1c, How dare you?!  How am I supposed to show up at the shows with a one-of-a-kind digital dash if you go showing everyone where to get it?! j/k. I've been looking into that dash for a while now.  Some other great things out of the same donor is the driver information center and the heads up display....<P>too bad it's blue, the red dash is one of the things I love about my fiero...||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||06-15-2001||10:03 AM||||Check out the gauges @ Pisa <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/dgauges.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/dgauges.html</A> <P>The guy who make these for Pisa is a member of my Fiero club (Suncoast Fiero - St. Pete, FL) and they a great. He is an Electrical Engineer and stands firmly behind his product. For those who went to the Daytona show, he was demonstrating the gauges at the Holiday Inn at the reception the night before the show.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||p4n1c||06-15-2001||10:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>Some other great things out of the same donor is the driver information center and the heads up display....<P>too bad it's blue, the red dash is one of the things I love about my fiero...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have to remember to hide my dash when Fiero owners come near the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't want it going missing.  My car didn't come with the Driver Info Center, the only option it didn't have, but I'm looking into getting it.  Heads up display?  I don't remember seeing that, is it on the newer models?<P>Yeah, it's vaccuum filled aqua LCD.  There's no real way of changing the colour to red, you could probably get other colours by masking it.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000008||elfiero||06-15-2001||11:06 AM||||Maybe someone out there knows more about this<BR>than me but,every one of those "factory"type<BR>didgital dashes need a BCM to support them to<BR>operate correctly.i-e,the sensors signals go<BR>to the BCM which converts the signals to<BR>didgital-which the "cluster"displays.I'm not<BR>totally sure about this,so somebody speak up!||||reg||6
Z||000009||fierogt88||06-15-2001||11:18 AM||||The Cutlass uses a 3.1, the cousin to our 2.8.  I was planning on grabbing all the electronics together.  I found a dash in the junkyard this weekend with everything _except_ the digital dash itself.  The HUD was a box that sat on top of the dash.  I found this one in a 93 International in good shape.  I don't know if it was the only year with the HUD, but I passed on it since the dash itself was gone.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Greg Piet||06-15-2001||11:31 AM||||I LOVE Cliffs setup, with on exception.<BR>I do not have the Rally Pod, but I do have an oil pressure gaugein with the Tach.<P>From my readings Cliffs setup does not have an oil pressure gauge in the main part of the dash.  Because of this Cliffs gauge set will have to wait till I have a rally pod(which will be a bloody long time).<P>I believe cliffs also uses the Speedo to calculate 0-60 and 60-0 times as well as 1/4 miles times...<BR>All it needs is an accelerometer and its an onboard integrated performance monitoring system||||reg||1
Z||000011||p4n1c||06-15-2001||02:10 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>The Cutlass uses a 3.1, the cousin to our 2.8.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well mine uses the exact same engine(2.8 with same intake and exhaust lift), except it has DIS and is more restrictive(air intake is a 3" high by 2" opening behind the headlight).  But I believe it just has a sending unit to send the information to the dash.  But there are digital sensors for speed, etc.  It sends pulses to the computer which are converted to speed, which is why I can do 15-20kph in park.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The HUD must've been a new thing to the '93.  Which makes sense since my Chilton's only covers 88-92.  I do want to get the drivers information center though.  It's fun to play with.<P>EDIT: The '92+ International and maybe the '91 used a DOHC 3.4L 210hp V6.  Fast bugger and made up for the weight of the car(mine is 3200lbs curb weight, the engine is underpowered for the car, still pulls it pretty good though).<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||1
